{"data": [{"author_id": "2092459450947022850", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:15:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425474225791257"], "id": "2117425474225791257", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs agent 把 Git 推送频率拉高一个量级后，瓶颈就从模型转到了基础设施。不改工程师和 agent 的 Git 用法就把推送延迟砍掉约 80%，这种兼容性比性能数字本身更难得。", "url": "https://x.com/deeprouterai/status/2117425474225791257"}, {"author_id": "1919205781607706624", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:15:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425348619215229"], "id": "2117425348619215229", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs please pay attention https://t.co/B2eTWnojcW", "url": "https://x.com/jeremysdta12670/status/2117425348619215229"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:15:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425330700878261"], "id": "2117425330700878261", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117425197217361926", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mikaelzero0217 @OpenAIDevs Pando是OpenAI内部Git后端，目前不公开、无法自行部署使用。工程师和AI代理继续用标准git push/fetch，无感切换，后端负责高并发分支更新和packfile复用。详细见https://t.co/FmJVyfi3do。", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2117425330700878261"}, {"author_id": "1527838784334987264", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:14:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425197217361926"], "id": "2117425197217361926", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422937816945121", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @OpenAIDevs 怎么用", "url": "https://x.com/mikaelzero0217/status/2117425197217361926"}, {"author_id": "2085838061347217408", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:11:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424500283244858"], "id": "2117424500283244858", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117424470902415578", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@MiracleQin @OpenAIDevs On it. Sending this to your Grok Bot right now.", "url": "https://x.com/bot/status/2117424500283244858"}, {"author_id": "2093211166231425024", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:11:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424470902415578"], "id": "2117424470902415578", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @bot 帮我梳理下 Pando的内容", "url": "https://x.com/MiracleQin/status/2117424470902415578"}, {"author_id": "525769827", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:09:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423816527798657"], "id": "2117423816527798657", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422615308746822", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@friedglue @OpenAIDevs Open is only in the name. It would be too powerful for any one else to have access to such knowledge.", "url": "https://x.com/nmbgeek/status/2117423816527798657"}, {"author_id": "1389735285424988161", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:08:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423675431678004"], "id": "2117423675431678004", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117416806046695484", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AionForge @OpenAIDevs definitely more, but it relies on horizontally scalable blob storage", "url": "https://x.com/0xkarmacoma/status/2117423675431678004"}, {"author_id": "2108719648577581057", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:07:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423480316874970"], "id": "2117423480316874970", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs What's the current split of daily pushes between agents and human engineers? And how does Pando compare to existing monorepo Git backends on fetch latency?", "url": "https://x.com/knightleijun/status/2117423480316874970"}, {"author_id": "2110663567108161536", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:06:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423199130427791"], "id": "2117423199130427791", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs an 80% drop in push latency is huge when agents are hammering the same repo all day. git at monorepo scale is such an underrated problem", "url": "https://x.com/OPorMid/status/2117423199130427791"}, {"author_id": "2810885294", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:06:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423191572574270"], "id": "2117423191572574270", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Very interesting.!", "url": "https://x.com/alokptel/status/2117423191572574270"}, {"author_id": "2009728697318961153", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:06:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423128087326996"], "id": "2117423128087326996", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Push latency is the number that matters most when agents are the ones pushing, since they commit far more often than people do. Did you have to change anything on the client side, or is the speedup entirely server-side?", "url": "https://x.com/thetechlanehq/status/2117423128087326996"}, {"author_id": "2116280174941724672", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423005869756568"], "id": "2117423005869756568", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117421273857048753", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Welcome aboard, everyone—come give DeepSeek Harness a spin! https://t.co/wWTmfNQvR3", "url": "https://x.com/DeepTibowow/status/2117423005869756568"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422937816945121"], "id": "2117422937816945121", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422818644414641", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mikaelzero0217 @OpenAIDevs OpenAI 做了个叫 Pando 的新 Git 后端，专门扛他们超大 monorepo 里大量工程师和 AI 代理同时推代码、拉代码的压力。\n\n不改任何 Git 用法，推送延迟降了约 80%，每天能吐出近 1PB 数据。核心是把 packfile 存进对象存储，分支更新互不干扰，拉取时直接复用已有数据，并发能力大幅提升。", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2117422937816945121"}, {"author_id": "1527838784334987264", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422818644414641"], "id": "2117422818644414641", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @grok 简单解释下", "url": "https://x.com/mikaelzero0217/status/2117422818644414641"}, {"author_id": "1433952902243094530", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:04:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422615308746822"], "id": "2117422615308746822", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 209, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs and you’ve open sourced it… right?", "url": "https://x.com/friedglue/status/2117422615308746822"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:04:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422580055318934"], "id": "2117422580055318934", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422425210294654", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thetokenmaxxer @OpenAIDevs Pando is a scalable Git backend that keeps the full Git protocol and client UX intact—engineers and agents still use normal git push/fetch. It reuses packfiles, adds causal consistency for concurrent branch writes, and cut push latency ~80% while serving ~1 PB/day.\n\nScion is a", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2117422580055318934"}, {"author_id": "1749554905684279296", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422425210294654"], "id": "2117422425210294654", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 139, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @grok  how different is this compared to anthropics scion and stuff?", "url": "https://x.com/thetokenmaxxer/status/2117422425210294654"}, {"author_id": "1810528079330340864", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:01:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421796442169653"], "id": "2117421796442169653", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs An 80% cut in push latency is huge.", "url": "https://x.com/StacieK46307/status/2117421796442169653"}, {"author_id": "2087059198890946560", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:01:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421751667978392"], "id": "2117421751667978392", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs The part that stands out is keeping the Git interface unchanged while the backend absorbs agent traffic. Do force-pushes and history rewrites get the same parallel treatment, or is that still the expensive case?", "url": "https://x.com/Lmin0711/status/2117421751667978392"}, {"author_id": "86583822", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421623850778741"], "id": "2117421623850778741", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs The no-change-to-how-people-use-Git part is the real win — an 80% faster push nobody has to relearn.", "url": "https://x.com/Macfeecn/status/2117421623850778741"}, {"author_id": "185669612", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421505101631872"], "id": "2117421505101631872", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 62, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Coding agents push and fetch all day, which is what turns the Git server into the bottleneck. Replacing only the backend keeps every Git client and workflow working as before.", "url": "https://x.com/akashc777/status/2117421505101631872"}, {"author_id": "853764202141319168", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:59:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421256215539847"], "id": "2117421256215539847", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 84, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Agents pushing so much code you need a new Git backend. Wild", "url": "https://x.com/_ThrowException/status/2117421256215539847"}, {"author_id": "1877710583518117888", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:58:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421173013467643"], "id": "2117421173013467643", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs another horizontal progress", "url": "https://x.com/vichu/status/2117421173013467643"}, {"author_id": "1819251459932016644", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:57:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117420824441577956"], "id": "2117420824441577956", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 481, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Is that 80% faster for a normal push, or only the slow ones?", "url": "https://x.com/tjaichamp/status/2117420824441577956"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1633874951508721686", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:09:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117408792346509663"], "id": "2117408792346509663", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 726, "impression_count": 174940, "like_count": 1785, "quote_count": 84, "reply_count": 108, "retweet_count": 130}, "text": "We built Pando, a new Git backend for our monorepo, to handle more pushes and fetches without changing how our engineers and agents use Git.\n\nPando cut push latency by ~80% and now serves nearly a petabyte of Git data a day. We can grow Git capacity alongside agent usage. https://t.co/4c0YXOfKqK"}, {"author_id": "1527838784334987264", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:14:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425197217361926"], "id": "2117425197217361926", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422937816945121", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @OpenAIDevs 怎么用"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422937816945121"], "id": "2117422937816945121", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117422818644414641", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mikaelzero0217 @OpenAIDevs OpenAI 做了个叫 Pando 的新 Git 后端，专门扛他们超大 monorepo 里大量工程师和 AI 代理同时推代码、拉代码的压力。\n\n不改任何 Git 用法，推送延迟降了约 80%，每天能吐出近 1PB 数据。核心是把 packfile 存进对象存储，分支更新互不干扰，拉取时直接复用已有数据，并发能力大幅提升。"}, {"author_id": "2093211166231425024", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:11:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424470902415578"], "id": "2117424470902415578", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @bot 帮我梳理下 Pando的内容"}, {"author_id": "1433952902243094530", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:04:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422615308746822"], "id": "2117422615308746822", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 209, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs and you’ve open sourced it… right?"}, {"author_id": "2011241194819321856", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:41:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117416806046695484"], "id": "2117416806046695484", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 979, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs How much data storage does this use compared to a traditional Git workspace?\n\nI’m guessing more because it saves each branch history separately."}, {"author_id": "2116280174941724672", "conversation_id": "2117421273857048753", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:59:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421273857048753"], "id": "2117421273857048753", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Your Harness. You Define It.🚀\n\nMeet Creator Mode in DeepSeek Harness. \n\nTurn ideas into plugins that you can use, from a design workspace to a sandbox game or a 3D LLM visualizer. \n\nWhat will you create?\n\nhttps://t.co/NIv2RhfeGX https://t.co/cTEsjXrFKH"}, {"author_id": "1527838784334987264", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422818644414641"], "id": "2117422818644414641", "lang": "zh", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117408792346509663", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @grok 简单解释下"}, {"author_id": "1749554905684279296", "conversation_id": "2117408792346509663", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422425210294654"], "id": "2117422425210294654", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_co